or for the two Americans.

257
00:11:34.569 --> 00:11:36.071
the trunk of the car.

258
00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:40.574
Main charge sits low
on the gas tank.

259
00:11:40.575 --> 00:11:43.452
We'll layer it.
Two kilos in total.

260
00:11:43.453 --> 00:11:46.455
It'll peel the car open
like a sardine tin.

261
00:11:46.456 --> 00:11:47.958
Donal. you explain the rest.

262
00:11:49.459 --> 00:11:51.001
This is the blasting cap.

263
00:11:51.002 --> 00:11:52.753
Czech-made. fast fuse.

264
00:11:52.754 --> 00:11:55.172
Runs to this receiver.

265
00:11:55.173 --> 00:11:56.174
What about the trigger?

266
00:11:57.259 --> 00:11:59.176
We use this:

267
00:11:59.177 --> 00:12:01.637
a garage door remote.
nothing fancy.

268
00:12:01.638 --> 00:12:04.807
So you tune the receiver
to match the VHF frequency?

269
00:12:04.808 --> 00:12:07.476
Yes. but you'll need
a clear line of sight.

270
00:12:07.477 --> 00:12:11.021
It's not that strong.
Say. half a block away.

271
00:12:11.022 --> 00:12:12.231
What if the signal gets blocked?

272
00:12:12.232 --> 00:12:13.524
Then the garage doors
don't open.

273
00:12:13.525 --> 00:12:15.151
That's not gonna happen.

274
00:12:15.152 --> 00:12:17.236
I'll be less half a block
away from Markham.

275
00:12:17.237 --> 00:12:18.904
Signal will be strong and clear.

276
00:12:18.905 --> 00:12:21.115
Besides. I want the last thing

277
00:12:21.116 --> 00:12:23.410
that bastard see
to be my grinnin' face.

278
00:12:25.078 --> 00:12:26.746
I don't think
that's a good idea. Brendan.

279
00:12:27.706 --> 00:12:31.750
Colonel Markham personally
interrogated you in Maze Prison.

280
00:12:31.751 --> 00:12:34.211
I told you. I'm not gonna
go anywhere near him.

281
00:12:34.212 --> 00:12:36.714
No. Someone else should do it.
It's plain and simple.

282
00:12:36.715 --> 00:12:39.425
Oh. That someone else is you?

283
00:12:39.426 --> 00:12:41.678
My whole family died
at Markham's hands.

284
00:12:42.846 --> 00:12:44.347
Let him die at mine.

285
00:12:48.059 --> 00:12:49.435
All right.

286
00:12:49.436 --> 00:12:52.355
Nine. ten.

287
00:12:54.983 --> 00:12:57.486
All right. That's another
thousand right there.

288
00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:05.576
Wait. Is that it?
That's all of it?

289
00:13:05.577 --> 00:13:08.329
That's it. Jimmy.
That's everything.

290
00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.456
No. no. no. no. no.
We're short.

291
00:13:10.457 --> 00:13:12.458
I mean. we're really
fucking short. Mickey.

292
00:13:12.459 --> 00:13:14.168
-How is that possible?
-Well. 'cause unlike

293
00:13:14.169 --> 00:13:15.878
the motherfucker
that you call boss.

294
00:13:15.879 --> 00:13:18.339
who takes his fucking kickbacks
and keeps it all for himself.

295
00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:20.508
you're actually generous
with your people.

296
00:13:20.509 --> 00:13:22.134
Yeah. well. maybe I wouldn't
have been so fuckin' generous

297
00:13:22.135 --> 00:13:23.552
if I knew that was
all we were gonna take.

298
00:13:23.553 --> 00:13:25.555
-I know.
-Shit!

299
00:13:27.349 --> 00:13:28.974
All right. well.
look. look. we're starting

300
00:13:28.975 --> 00:13:31.393
a new business here.
This shit happens. right?

301
00:13:31.394 --> 00:13:33.270
So maybe we're too generous
with too many people.

302
00:13:33.271 --> 00:13:35.314
and maybe we had
a bit too much fun.

303
00:13:35.315 --> 00:13:38.025
We know now. next time
we'll tighten it up.

304
00:13:38.026 --> 00:13:40.861
Thing we do know is that
we can make real fuckin' money.

305
00:13:40.862 --> 00:13:43.447
It's just... it's just...
it's overheads. right?

306
00:13:43.448 --> 00:13:45.075
Fuckin' overheads.

307
00:13:46.284 --> 00:13:48.619
Shit. we're not gonna have
enough for that key for Tad.

308
00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:49.912
I mean. that knucklehead
was gonna spend

309
00:13:49.913 --> 00:13:51.455
a hundred grand on one key.

310
00:13:51.456 --> 00:13:53.249
That woulda been
a big fuckin' score. Mickey.

311
00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.042
All right.

312
00:13:55.043 --> 00:13:57.711
So. we take
Sweeney's fuckin' cut.

313
00:13:57.712 --> 00:13:59.296
-and we use that for our blow.
-No. no. no. no. no. no. no.

314
00:13:59.297 --> 00:14:00.798
We cannot fuckin' do that.

315
00:14:00.799 --> 00:14:03.467
-Why not?
-You know why not.

316
00:14:03.468 --> 00:14:05.761
Look. I'll talk to Sweeney.

317
00:14:05.762 --> 00:14:07.012
and who knows?

318
00:14:07.013 --> 00:14:08.764
Maybe he's feeling generous.

319
00:14:08.765 --> 00:14:10.641
Yeah. right.

320
00:14:15.146 --> 00:14:17.773
Not a bad day at the office.

321
00:14:17.774 --> 00:14:20.442
Business has been
pretty fuckin' great so far.

322
00:14:20.443 --> 00:14:23.863
The new Dominican contact
we found. it's popular.

323
00:14:24.864 --> 00:14:26.949
But. uh. we're gonna
need more coke

324
00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.450
if you wanna keep this going.

325
00:14:28.451 --> 00:14:30.369
How's your cash flow?

326
00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:33.789
Ah. well between
paying off the guys.

327
00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:37.376
and. uh. and you. and. um.

328
00:14:37.377 --> 00:14:39.837
you know. some of the supply
went for personal use.

329
00:14:39.838 --> 00:14:41.505
And I'm gonna be
a little bit short

330
00:14:41.506 --> 00:14:43.508
-for the next buy.
-Uh-huh.

331
00:14:45.719 --> 00:14:49.555
Um. so. what
I was wondering was.

332
00:14:49.556 --> 00:14:52.349
you know. if you could
just front us some cash.

333
00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:53.643
including what I just gave you.

334
00:14:57.856 --> 00:15:00.316
Not easy running
your own business. is it?

335
00:15:00.317 --> 00:15:03.027
You gotta handle inventory.

336
00:15:03.028 --> 00:15:04.570
watch your guys
like a fuckin' hawk.

337
00:15:04.571 --> 00:15:06.322
I guarantee you
at least one of your guys

338
00:15:06.323 --> 00:15:07.948
